# Register range operands (V8 RegList+RegCount, RegOutPair, RegOutTriple).
# rangeSrc/pair/triple set rStart/rEnd (first/last operand byte); rangeDst prints the range the
# way V8's disassembler does, e.g. "r1-r3" or "a1-a0". Consecutive registers of a V8 range have
# decreasing operand bytes, so the payloads expand it by stepping from rStart towards rEnd.
# (Replaces a 124-level recursive chain that overflowed SLEIGH's constructor depth limit of 64.)
rangeDst: "{}" is counter = 0 {}
rangeDst: rStart^"-"^rEnd is rStart & rEnd {}
# second copy, for instructions with two ranges
rangeDstStub: rangeDst is rangeDst {}
